From c2c215614066637e27a93ab02dd6048e3a6d020a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:36:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: apply the Necromancer lit-square penalty on any lit
 square

The game adds 25 to a Necromancer's spell failure chance whenever the
player's square is lit (square_islit(): torchlight, permanent room light,
bright terrain or a lit monster nearby). The Borg's estimate added it
only when the square was lit by the Borg's own light source, so a
Necromancer without a light standing in a lit room believed its spells
were far safer than they were. With Vampire Strike at a real 33% chance
of failure it estimated 8%, passed its own 25% limit and cast it anyway.

Use the same lit-square test the game uses.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#296.

(cherry picked from commit ea838de6782149c83300dccdfc06d15c099fbd86)
---
 src/borg/borg-magic.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-magic.c b/src/borg/borg-magic.c
index 1f476dc38..9598d0a48 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-magic.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-magic.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 
 #ifdef ALLOW_BORG
 
+#include "../cave.h"
 #include "../effects.h"
 #include "../player-spell.h"
 #include "../ui-menu.h"
@@ -528,10 +529,10 @@ int borg_spell_fail_rate(const enum borg_spells spell)
             minfail = 5;
     }
 
-    /* Necromancers are punished by being on lit squares */
-    /* necromancers like the dark */
+    /* Necromancers are punished by being on lit squares, whatever lights
+     * them (their own light, permanent light, a monster's light) */
     if (borg.trait[BI_CLASS] == CLASS_NECROMANCER &&
-        borg_grids[borg.c.y][borg.c.x].info & BORG_LIGHT) {
+        square_islit(cave, borg.c)) {
         chance += 25;
 
     }
